**Read:** Complete the introductory wastewater volumes and the selected full process books, with the graduate exercises in [Water and Wastewater Treatment Engineering — MIT 1.85](../sources/Water-and-Wastewater-Treatment-Engineering-MIT.lingua#r_396YEC55H29CR6J4ZBZX5JBY60). Use [Biological Wastewater Treatment — Chen and colleagues, second edition](../sources/Biological-Wastewater-Treatment-Chen-and-Colleagues.lingua#r_1AE9DK0YWQR5GDECZ9KK1JJP37), [Nutrient Control Design Manual — US EPA](../sources/Nutrient-Control-Design-Manual-EPA.lingua#r_5MZ6AJ5ZW61R793FSA311WAJ2G) and [Assessment of Treatment Plant Performance and Water Quality Data — von Sperling, Verbyla and Oliveira](../sources/Treatment-Plant-Performance-and-Water-Quality-Data.lingua#r_5PZG8VN422GHD657FBDR5KRWGS) for the advanced study and [Sanitation safety planning — WHO, second edition](../sources/Sanitation-Safety-Planning-WHO.lingua#r_2FF0R519TGR5RNY3EVV7APPZ86) for the complete service argument.

Present one connected account from contributors and collection through liquid treatment, solids handling and receiving routes. Explain it first without unexplained specialist terms, then defend the equations, sampling, kinetics, separation evidence, uncertainties and continuing work. Include a decentralized or alternative configuration so that a large centralized plant is not silently treated as the only possible service.

**Work:** Demonstrate independently checked balances and numerical examples, a reproducible hydraulic or process investigation, and a critical reading of primary operational evidence. Evaluate a changed influent, a power interruption, a failed separator and loss of a residual destination. Show how consequences cross unit boundaries and which observations would require revision of your explanation.

For scholarly completion of this section, reproduce an identified study, compare a competing model or interpretation, and defend an original extension against evidence withheld from fitting. Report what was actually read, calculated, observed or performed. Continue into industrial reuse, utility interfaces, whole-system operation and the final integrated studies. The wastewater investigation contributes to that wider account.
**Continue:** [Water quality begins with the service it must deliver](../industrial/Water-quality-begins-with-the-service-it-must-deliver.lingua#r_1EHYC601AFFNZ9FBF8J1Z9EPC8).

